Z||000005||daved||01-27-2000||11:10 PM||||Dough,  I can show you how to wire up your stuff...audio, fogs, neons etc.  Esentially, the power from the battery goes to a heavy buss at the rear of the fuse panel, passes through the various fuses, then on to your equipment.  If you were to hook up to the battery side of the fuse, you would have no protection against a short (and a small fire would ensue!!)  The fuse is a weak link to protect the wiring ( same as in your house...though newer ones use breakers, which are still a weak link).<BR>As far as the neon -12Volt supply: it just means you will have to islolate any metal part of the neon from the chassis of the car.  The neg. and Pos. are reversed in the neon electronics (though I have no idea why a manufacturer would do that for something sold in N. America)<BR>Hope you have a heavy-duty battery, and the high output alternator, to supply all the extra 'juice' your goodies are going to take,<BR>Dave||||reg||1
